    "title": "The 39 km Strait That Controls World Oil 🛢️🌍🤯 Strait of Hormuz",
    "description": "The Strait of Hormuz is only about 39 km wide at its narrowest 🌊 but around 25% of the world's seaborne oil trade and 20% of its liquefied natural gas pass through it 🛢️ It separates Iran 🇮🇷 from Oman's Musandam Peninsula 🇴🇲 and the shipping lanes are just 2 nautical miles wide in each direction 🚢 For countries like Qatar, Bahrain, Kuwait and Iraq it's the only sea route to the open ocean 🤯",
